%% ============================================
%% FRONTISPIECE — "全書一句話": the jars-of-clay verse (4:7) as
%% the single root beneath the letter's whole arc, from affliction
%% to power made perfect in weakness.
%% ============================================
\thispagestyle{empty}
\begin{center}
\vspace*{0.3in}

\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[ScriptureGold, line width=0.8pt] (-2.8,0) -- (-0.55,0);
  \fill[ScriptureGold] (0,0) circle (0.055);
  \draw[ScriptureGold, line width=0.8pt] (0.55,0) -- (2.8,0);
\end{tikzpicture}

\vspace{0.22cm}
{\Large\bfseries\color{ThornRed} 全書一句話 \textperiodcentered\ The Whole Book in One Sentence}

\vspace{0.30cm}
\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{ScriptureBg}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\centering\vspace{0.2cm}
\normalsize\color{TextGray}
我們有這\textbf{\color{JesusRed}寶貝}放在\textbf{\color{JesusRed}瓦器}裏，\\
要顯明這莫大的能力是出於神，不是出於我們。\\[0.5em]
\footnotesize\itshape
But we have this treasure in \textbf{\color{JesusRed}earthen vessels}, so that the surpassing\\
greatness of the power will be of God and not from ourselves.\\[0.4em]
\small\color{ThornRed} 哥林多後書 4:7 \textperiodcentered\ 2 Corinthians 4:7
\vspace{0.2cm}
\end{minipage}}

\vspace{0.35cm}
{\small\color{TextGray} 全書不是保羅的辯護狀，是一份十字架的自傳——患難、瓦器、軟弱，都不是事奉的障礙，是能力顯明的地方。\\
\textit{Not a defense brief, but a cross-shaped autobiography — affliction, clay, and weakness are not obstacles to ministry but exactly where power is displayed.}}

\vspace{0.30cm}
{\small
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.3}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{4.0cm}p{2.6cm}p{4.2cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{處境 Situation} & \textbf{看似 It Looks Like} & \textbf{領受 What Is Received} \\
\midrule
患難、瓦器、身上的刺 \newline {\scriptsize\itshape affliction, clay jars, the thorn} & 事奉的攔阻 \newline {\scriptsize\itshape a hindrance to ministry} & 能力顯明的舞台 \newline {\scriptsize\itshape the very stage on which power is displayed} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{ScriptureGold}{\rule{2.5in}{0.7pt}}
\vspace{0.3cm}

{\bfseries\color{ThornRed} 讀經之鑰 \textperiodcentered\ How to Read This Book}

\vspace{0.18cm}
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\small\color{TextGray}
每一章的處境都不一樣——患難、飽受質疑、奉獻的呼召、身上的刺——但保羅每次都把讀者帶回同一個地方——\\
不是自己的資格，乃是基督的十架與復活的大能。\\
讀這封信，不要只停在「保羅在為自己辯護甚麼」，\\
要問：這處境裏的軟弱，如何正是恩典顯明的地方？\\[0.5em]
\textit{\footnotesize
Each chapter's situation looks different — affliction, suspicion, the call to give, a thorn in the flesh —\\
but Paul keeps leading the reader back to the same place:\\
not his own credentials, but the cross and resurrection power of Christ.\\
Don't just ask what Paul is defending;\\
ask how the weakness in this situation is exactly where grace is displayed.}
\end{minipage}

\vfill
{\scriptsize\color{LightGray} PubHub 三書精讀系統 \textperiodcentered\ Soli Deo Gloria}

\vspace{0.3in}
\end{center}
